WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Tuesday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.360
the seventeenth of November.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.560
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.840
Two tankers were attacked in
the Strait of Hormuz on Monday,

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.760
and this time the attacks are confirmed
by maritime security warnings,

6
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.760
not just Iranian claims.
Even so, oil fell,

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.840
as forecasts of a supply glut
outweighed the risk in the Gulf.

8
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.360
On the markets. Oil fell more
than three percent on Monday,

9
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.280
according to Rigzone. On Monday
morning, Brent was down two point three

10
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.680
percent at ninety-three dollars
sixty, according to OilPrice dot com.

11
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.440
Murban moved the other way, up one
point five percent to ninety-four

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.200
dollars ninety. Front-month
Title Transfer Facility gas,

13
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.720
Europe's benchmark, fell three point
three percent to about eighty-eight

14
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.040
euros a megawatt hour. European
Union storage stood at seventy point

15
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.600
four percent full as of Sunday.

16
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.840
Starting in the Gulf. United Kingdom
Maritime Trade Operations issued

17
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.800
separate warnings about two tankers
attacked in Hormuz on Monday.

18
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.467
Both had engine-room fires,
and one was left disabled.

19
00:01:05.573 --> 00:01:08.040
Recent hits had rested
on Iran's word alone,

20
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.760
so this is the first maritime-security
confirmation of attacks on a single

21
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:12.747
day.

22
00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:15.720
Iran's Revolutionary Guards
tell their own story.

23
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.600
They say two tankers struck mines on
Monday after taking a southern route

24
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.680
Iran has not authorised, and that US
officers guided them with fighter-jet

25
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.720
support. That account is Iran's alone.

26
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.840
The reports don't name an attacker,
and it isn't clear whether these

27
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.840
are the same two ships. Statements
from the owners or flag states would

28
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.093
settle it.

29
00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:38.520
Iran also struck Bahrain for
the second time in three days,

30
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.240
Rigzone reported, while saying a
path to ending the conflict remains

31
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.880
open. The market barely flinched,
and one account carried by gCaptain

32
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.960
says the war hasn't stopped
crude reaching buyers.

33
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.813
For owners of supertankers, the
risk premium is unwinding fast,

34
00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:57.413
with rates down more than sixty
percent from October's record.

35
00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:00.680
Down the coast, the Red Sea
route is under new pressure.

36
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.320
Yemeni military sources say Houthi
fighters are within a hundred kilometres

37
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.920
of Aden after government forces pulled
back from positions near the Bab

38
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.627
el-Mandeb. The Houthis have
not given their own account.

39
00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:15.120
The strait matters because Saudi
crude loaded at Yanbu passes through

40
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.800
it on the way to Asia. Yanbu is
the outlet that bypasses Hormuz.

41
00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.960
Any threat there reaches the very
barrels that have been replacing Gulf

42
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.200
loadings, and that is the backdrop
to Murban gaining while Brent fell.

43
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.480
Container lines, meanwhile,
are heading the other way:

44
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.960
Maersk and Hapag-Lloyd are returning
three more Gemini services to Suez,

45
00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.160
according to gCaptain.

46
00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.240
Turning to the supply picture.

47
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.320
The EIA now expects a global
oil glut this quarter.

48
00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.040
Goldman Sachs goes further, seeing
supply exceeding demand by two million

49
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.440
barrels a day in twenty twenty-seven.

50
00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.640
It expects Brent to average
eighty-eight dollars next year,

51
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.440
then slide toward
seventy-eight by year-end,

52
00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.360
citing weaker Chinese
demand for transport fuel.

53
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.320
New barrels keep arriving.

54
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.880
ExxonMobil has started Uaru, its
fifth project on the Stabroek block,

55
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.040
World Oil reported. That lifts Guyana's
installed capacity to one point

56
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.040
one million barrels a day.

57
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.520
Gulf crude is getting cheaper to buy.

58
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.840
Kpler reports deeper discounts on
Mideast Gulf grades as Asian refiners

59
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.680
turn to Atlantic barrels.

60
00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.520
Chinese independent refiners are
chasing Iraqi cargoes through trading

61
00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.680
houses, Bloomberg reported, because
the US blockade has halted Iranian

62
00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.720
supply and Russian
crude has become dearer.

63
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.840
Iraq is also trucking
crude out through Syria.

64
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.200
Refined products haven't
followed crude all the way down.

65
00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.000
US diesel has dropped
below six dollars a gallon,

66
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.920
according to OilPrice dot com.

67
00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.680
Jet fuel stays high, though, and
that lands on airlines just as their

68
00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.440
price hedges expire.

69
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:52.560
Now to gas. Pipeline flows to US
liquefied natural gas plants hit a record

70
00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.720
twenty-one point eight billion
cubic feet on Saturday,

71
00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.640
according to BloombergNEF.

72
00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.213
That's up twelve percent on a year ago.

73
00:04:00.347 --> 00:04:04.760
Golden Pass set a record, and Sabine
Pass reached its highest since April.

74
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.800
Add milder weather forecasts, and that
explains Monday's slide in European

75
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:09.880
prices.

76
00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.120
Storage is still the constraint.

77
00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.560
EU stocks slipped about two
tenths of a point on Sunday.

78
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.000
According to APA-Economics, net
withdrawals so far equal about a tenth

79
00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:24.280
of the fifty-one point two billion
cubic metres injected this summer.

80
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.840
UK supply news cuts both ways.

81
00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.600
Gas from Jackdaw is now flowing
to St Fergus through Shearwater,

82
00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.667
according to the operator Adura.

83
00:04:32.693 --> 00:04:36.320
But the Apache pay dispute has
escalated to a standstill on its North

84
00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.840
Sea platforms, Offshore Energy reported,
and no volumes have been given.

85
00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.853
In Norway, the Supreme Court has
invalidated approvals for Breidablikk,

86
00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.880
Tyrving and Yggdrasil over
their emissions assessments,

87
00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.040
according to Splash twenty-four seven.

88
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.387
A few more things.

89
00:04:51.413 --> 00:04:54.920
The EU's new Russia sanctions
package targets the shipowners,

90
00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.840
managers, insurers and financial
networks behind the shadow fleet,

91
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.400
gCaptain reported. Going after
insurance and management,

92
00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.680
not just hulls, shrinks the services
Russian cargoes can draw on.

93
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:11.200
Separately, a Somali-flagged wheat
carrier capsized off Bulgaria after

94
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.880
a reported sea-drone attack.

95
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.440
Chevron and Iraq's oil minister have
both now confirmed agreed contract

96
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.600
terms for West Qurna 2, which until
now had been Baghdad's claim alone.

97
00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.880
Canadian Natural is buying Advantage
Energy for one point eight billion

98
00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.080
US dollars including
debt, World Oil reported.

99
00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.880
The deal adds about seventy-nine
thousand barrels of oil equivalent a

100
00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:34.640
day.

101
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.640
Diamondback is buying Double Eagle
subsidiaries for two point one five

102
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.200
billion dollars in cash plus stock.

103
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.760
And a KKR-led group is raising its
stake in Sempra Infrastructure to

104
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.240
sixty-five percent.

105
00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.600
What to watch next. Wednesday
brings the EIA weekly report,

106
00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.680
covering the week to the
thirteenth of November.

107
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.680
Distillate stocks stood at about one
hundred and three point three million

108
00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.160
barrels the week before. And the
daily EU gas storage readings from Gas

109
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.720
Infrastructure Europe run
through the twenty-fourth.

110
00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.120
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
